---
import AwesomeGithubLayout from "../../layouts/AwesomeGithubLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;

const buildingBlocks = [
  {
    icon: "📝",
    name: "Instructions",
    description: "Canonical coding standards, accessibility, and documentation formats.",
  },
  {
    icon: "🤖",
    name: "Agents",
    description: "Specialized AI agents for code review, release, branding, and planning.",
  },
  {
    icon: "⚡",
    name: "Skills",
    description: "Portable, self-contained skill packages with SKILL.md entrypoints.",
  },
  {
    icon: "⚙️",
    name: "Workflows",
    description: "Portable agentic workflow spaces, each paired with an integration point.",
  },
  {
    icon: "🛠️",
    name: "Hooks",
    description: "Pre-commit and post-commit guardrails that enforce quality before code lands.",
  },
  {
    icon: "🔧",
    name: "Tools",
    description: "The tool-chain layer — AI utilities, scripts, schemas, and editor configs.",
  },
];

const adoptionSteps = [
  {
    number: 1,
    title: "Set the context",
    description: "Enable a central repository — ours is .github — as the source of truth for governance.",
  },
  {
    number: 2,
    title: "Pull in the right assets",
    description: "Copy .github-native portable assets into your .github/. You control what to install.",
  },
  {
    number: 3,
    title: "Land Copilot instructions",
    description: "Teach your Copilot — and your team — the rules by landing instruction files.",
  },
  {
    number: 4,
    title: "Read and iterate",
    description: "Review results. Work out what lands well and what doesn't. Rinse and repeat.",
  },
];
---

<AwesomeGithubLayout
  title="Getting Started — Awesome GitHub"
  description="Understand the control plane philosophy and adoption model."
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="ag-hero-large">
    <div class="ag-container">
      <h1 class="ag-h1">
        <span class="ag-hero-line-1">One .github repo</span>
        <span class="ag-hero-line-2">to rule them all.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="ag-lead">
        A central control plane owns governance — rules, workflows, instructions, agents. Resources cascade to every repository automatically. No copy-paste drift. No version skew.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Drift Section -->
  <section class="ag-section-alt">
    <div class="ag-container">
      <div class="ag-content-grid">
        <div class="ag-content-text">
          <h2 class="ag-h2">Drift, at agency scale</h2>
          <p>
            WordPress teams scaled repositories faster than standards. Triage drifted. Workflows weren't consistent. Release discipline got loose. Operational drag crept in.
          </p>
          <p>
            The deeper problem: governance files lived in every repository. When a standard changed, you edited a hundred copies. When a policy shifted, you re-triage a thousand issues. Culture and coordination exhausted engineering.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ag-content-highlight">
          <blockquote>
            "How do you sync governance across 40 repositories when your team is 6 people and you're shipping features?"
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Control Plane Section -->
  <section class="ag-section">
    <div class="ag-container">
      <div class="ag-content-grid ag-content-grid-reversed">
        <div class="ag-content-text">
          <h2 class="ag-h2">A control plane, not a folder</h2>
          <p>
            The breakthrough was centralising governance. One .github repository became the source of truth: issue templates, labels, workflows, instructions, agents, hooks, and reusable assets all defined once.
          </p>
          <p>
            But a central repo is only the first step. The real magic happens when you treat it as a <strong>control plane</strong>, not a folder. Each resource type is portable. Labels are importable. Instructions auto-land. Agents run on a schedule. Hooks cascade to every repository automatically.
          </p>
          <p>
            This eliminates the core problem: <strong>no copy-paste, no version skew, no stale governance.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ag-content-highlight">
          <code>github.com/lightspeedwp/.github</code>
          <p>The control plane is the single source of truth for how we code, test, release, and govern.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Building Blocks Section -->
  <section class="ag-section-alt">
    <div class="ag-container">
      <h2 class="ag-h2">The building blocks</h2>
      <p class="ag-lead">
        The control plane is built from six layers. Each is atomic, portable, and independently useful.
      </p>
      <div class="ag-blocks-grid">
        {buildingBlocks.map((block) => (
          <div class="ag-block-card">
            <div class="ag-block-icon">{block.icon}</div>
            <h3 class="ag-block-name">{block.name}</h3>
            <p class="ag-block-description">{block.description}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="ag-blocks-note">
        <p>
          The six layers form a coherent whole: instructions teach standards, agents enforce them, hooks guard them, skills extend them, workflows automate them, tools implement them. Together, they comprise the control plane.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- From Governance to Plugin Section -->
  <section class="ag-section">
    <div class="ag-container">
      <div class="ag-content-grid">
        <div class="ag-content-text">
          <h2 class="ag-h2">From governance to a plugin you install</h2>
          <p>
            Governance alone is not enough. As AI tooling expanded — Copilot, Claude, GitHub Actions, local hooks — we realised that a central repo was the source, but not the execution plane.
          </p>
          <p>
            We pivoted to an <strong>installable model</strong>. The .github repo remains the source of truth. But now, portable plugin packs carry capabilities to Copilot, to Claude Code, to local git hooks, and to CI/CD pipelines.
          </p>
          <p>
            This means: <strong>one source, many execution contexts. Standards, everywhere.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ag-content-highlight">
          <p>Install the control plane as a Copilot plugin. As a Claude skill pack. As a git hook. As a reusable workflow.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Adoption Section -->
  <section class="ag-section-alt">
    <div class="ag-container">
      <h2 class="ag-h2">Adopt it in four steps</h2>
      <div class="ag-adoption-grid">
        {adoptionSteps.map((step) => (
          <div class="ag-adoption-card">
            <div class="ag-adoption-number">{step.number}</div>
            <h3 class="ag-adoption-title">{step.title}</h3>
            <p class="ag-adoption-description">{step.description}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Horizon Section -->
  <section class="ag-section">
    <div class="ag-container">
      <h2 class="ag-h2">The horizon</h2>
      <p class="ag-lead">
        The control plane is designed to evolve. As standards clarify and tooling matures, we update the source once. Every repository, every tool, every context receives the update automatically.
      </p>
      <div class="ag-horizon-content">
        <p>
          The goal is not to build a monolithic system, but to establish a <strong>governance layer</strong> that is:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Inherited:</strong> Standards cascade automatically to every repository.</li>
          <li><strong>Portable:</strong> Capabilities work across any tool — GitHub, Copilot, Claude, local hooks.</li>
          <li><strong>Versioned:</strong> Changes are explicit, tested, and controlled. Teams opt in to new standards.</li>
          <li><strong>Human-centred:</strong> Automation amplifies human judgment; it never replaces it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</AwesomeGithubLayout>

<style>
  .ag-container {
    max-width: var(--container-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--gutter);
  }

  .ag-hero-large {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0F1014 0%, #181820 100%);
    color: var(--c-white);
    padding: var(--space-40) var(--gutter) var(--space-32);
  }

  .ag-h1 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h1);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    line-height: var(--lh-heading);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  .ag-hero-line-1 {
    display: block;
  }

  .ag-hero-line-2 {
    display: block;
    color: var(--c-light-blue);
  }

  .ag-h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    line-height: var(--lh-heading);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  .ag-lead {
    font-size: var(--fs-lead);
    line-height: var(--lh-loose);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8) 0;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .ag-section {
    padding: var(--space-40) var(--gutter);
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .ag-section-alt {
    padding: var(--space-40) var(--gutter);
    background: var(--bg-alt);
  }

  .ag-hero-large .ag-lead {
    color: var(--c-slate-300);
  }

  .ag-content-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .ag-content-grid-reversed {
    direction: rtl;
  }

  .ag-content-grid-reversed > * {
    direction: ltr;
  }

  .ag-content-text {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-loose);
  }

  .ag-content-text p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6) 0;
    color: var(--fg-2);
  }

  .ag-content-text p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .ag-content-text strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
  }

  .ag-content-highlight {
    padding: var(--space-6);
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--c-light-blue);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .ag-section-alt .ag-content-highlight {
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .ag-content-highlight blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-loose);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--fg-1);
  }

  .ag-content-highlight code {
    display: block;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    background: var(--bg-muted);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
    color: var(--c-light-blue);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .ag-section-alt .ag-content-highlight code {
    background: rgba(123, 231, 255, 0.1);
  }

  .ag-content-highlight p {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
    color: var(--fg-2);
  }

  .ag-blocks-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  .ag-block-card {
    padding: var(--space-6);
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    text-align: center;
    transition: all 0.2s ease-out;
  }

  .ag-section-alt .ag-block-card {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
  }

  .ag-block-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--c-light-blue);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(123, 231, 255, 0.1);
  }

  .ag-block-icon {
    font-size: 32px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .ag-block-name {
    font-size: var(--fs-h4);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) 0;
  }

  .ag-block-description {
    font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: var(--lh-snug);
  }

  .ag-blocks-note {
    padding: var(--space-6);
    background: rgba(123, 231, 255, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(123, 231, 255, 0.2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .ag-blocks-note p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-loose);
  }

  .ag-adoption-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .ag-adoption-card {
    padding: var(--space-8);
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .ag-section-alt .ag-adoption-card {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
  }

  .ag-adoption-number {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--c-light-blue);
    color: var(--c-black);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    font-size: var(--fs-h4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .ag-adoption-title {
    font-size: var(--fs-h4);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3) 0;
  }

  .ag-adoption-description {
    font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: var(--lh-loose);
  }

  .ag-horizon-content {
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .ag-horizon-content p {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-loose);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6) 0;
  }

  .ag-horizon-content ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 0 0 var(--space-6);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .ag-horizon-content li {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-loose);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .ag-horizon-content li::before {
    content: "→ ";
    color: var(--c-light-blue);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    margin-right: var(--space-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .ag-hero-large {
      padding: var(--space-20) var(--gutter) var(--space-16);
    }

    .ag-h1 {
      font-size: var(--fs-h2);
    }

    .ag-section,
    .ag-section-alt {
      padding: var(--space-20) var(--gutter);
    }

    .ag-content-grid,
    .ag-content-grid-reversed {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .ag-blocks-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .ag-adoption-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
        <p>
          Get a practical implementation sequence your teams can follow. Start with one outcome, roll
          out gradually.
        </p>
        <a href="/talk/slides/12/" class="inline-link">View in Slide 12 →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Quick Reference</h2>
    <div class="page-copy">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="/talk/">Talk Overview</a> — 25-minute presentation on .github governance
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/talk/slides/">All Slides</a> — Browse the 20 slides individually
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/agents/">Agent Guides</a> — Explore each of the 6 core agents
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/references/glossary/">Glossary</a> — Key terminology and definitions
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="/references/sources/">Sources & Tools</a> — Evidence and reference materials
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .learning-path {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .path-card {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    position: relative;
  }

  .step-number {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 2.5rem;
    height: 2.5rem;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-radius: 50%;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .path-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .path-card p {
    flex: 1;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .path-link {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: all 0.2s ease-out;
  }

  .path-link:hover {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: var(--bg);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .topic-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .topic-card {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .topic-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }

  .topic-card p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .learning-path,
    .topic-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
